## 3. Major Applications

| Domain | Key Mechanism & Importance |
| --- | --- |
| **Cryptography (ECC)** | Defines curves over finite fields ($\mathbb{F}_p$). The **Elliptic Curve Discrete Logarithm Problem (ECDLP)** makes computing $k$ from $P$ and $Q = kP$ computationally infeasible, enabling secure public-key encryption, ECDSA signatures, and TLS with significantly shorter key sizes than RSA. |
| **Number Theory** | Central to solving Diophantine equations. Andrew Wiles used the **Modularity Theorem**—which states that every elliptic curve over $\mathbb{Q}$ is parameterized by a modular form—to prove **Fermat's Last Theorem**. |
| **Theoretical Physics** | Used in string theory, integrable systems, and conformal field theory to compute partition functions and torus compactifications. |
